    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0383" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/852.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Admiral Osterhaus telegraphs the Navy Department as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Minister concurs with me in believing there is no need for ships here
                            and that the Third Division, Atlantic Fleet, with force on board, may
                            return north; also, in my opinion, state of affairs in the Province of
                            Oriente is such that all vessels of the Fourth Division, Atlantic Fleet,
                            may be withdrawn, leaving landed forces and gunboats to handle
                            situation. The latest reliable information indicates Cuban forces can
                            control situation.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Pursuant to this telegram the large war vessels at Key West, Habana and
                    Guantánamo have been ordered north; the gunboats, auxiliaries and marines to
                    remain. Inform consul at Santiago.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
